Things Needed for Autonomous Drone Project

Hardware:

Raspberry Pi 4 (8GB RAM)
64GB high-speed microSD card
Cooling fan and heatsink for Raspberry Pi
Camera (USB camera or Raspberry Pi Camera Module)
(Strongly recommended) Intel RealSense D435/D455 for depth sensing
USB cable or UART cable to connect Pixhawk and Raspberry Pi
External 5V BEC (clean power supply for Raspberry Pi)

🔸🔸🔸🔸🔸🔸🔸🔸🔸🔸🔸🔸🔸🔸

Software / Libraries:

Ubuntu 20.04 LTS (ARM64 for Raspberry Pi)
Python 3.8 or higher
OpenCV
YOLOv5 or YOLOv8 (lightweight model)
NumPy
Object tracking algorithm (CSRT / Centroid / SORT)
PID controller code for flight control
MAVLink protocol support
pymavlink
(Optional but recommended) ROS and MAVROS
Ground station software: QGroundControl or Mission Planner



